les are  properties within a blueprint that  either hold a value or reference an  actor within the world and sequencer is  the cinematic editor used within unreal  engine 4. it gives the ability to create  cinematics for the multi-track editor  and allows the user to use keyframes to  determine the content for the scene  controlling things like transformations  which moves things around  media audio and so much more  so let's take you through the things  that i learned that was new here and  that i think brought this music video to  life the first thing was lighting  this music video was set in a very small  space so lighting was extremely  important to do this i used a few  features within unreal engine that i  hadn't used previously to elevate the  lighting within my scene and allow me  more control over it number one real  time ray trace zen i got to turn that  bad boy on  now that i have a beasty pc i could use  real-time rage racing without having to  worry about whether my graphics card  could handle it if you're looking for an  easy way to get realistic lighting with  soft shadows you'll probably want to  turn this on within the render tab in  your project settings however i would  recommend  maybe duplicating your project if you're  not 100 certain that your pc graphics  card can handle it because it could just  crash your entire project and that's not  good for anyone the unreal engine  documentation states  ray tracing effects look more natural  producing soft shadowing for lights  accurate ambient occlusion ao  interactive global illumination  reflections and more  it look pretty two light ies textures my  scene had lots of small light sources  such as fairy lights and a candle  so i used ies textures to give a more  realistic lighting effects to display on  objects nearby these such as the walls  or other objects ies stands for  illuminating engineering society  profiles which are for a lighting  industry standard method of  demonstrating the brightness 